    "created_at": "2019-10-25T18:26:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-10-25T18:26:07Z",
    "body": "That's a good idea. This feature can help avoiding a lot of embarrassing situations at work, when people deploy stuff to production by mistake ;)\r\n\r\nWhile using Zsh + Spaceship, I added the feature there: https://github.com/denysdovhan/spaceship-prompt/pull/576\r\n\r\nNow that I switched to Bash and started using Starship, I'm kind of missing it. I looked at the code, but I never worked with Rust and it's a little confusing right now. I'll try to create a PR if I manage to get my head around this.\r\n\r\nWhat sort of matching do you think will work best for the `match` property?\r\nIMO Regex is an overkill, and something like glob or fnmatch should be good enough.\r\n\r\nThoughts?\r\n\r\n",
